// "you control [object]" ([CR#603.4] the common `Exists` intervening-if
// shape) — the controller-relative existence check a conditional static's
// "as long as you control an artifact" composes
// (`StaticEffect::Conditionally`, [CR#611.3a]): `Exists(And([And([Permanent,
// <object>]), ControlledBy(Ref(You))]))`. What you control is a permanent
// [CR#109.2]: a card you own in your hand, library or graveyard is not "an
// artifact you control". `Param(0)` is the object's own `Predicate`
// description (a bare card type, a creature-type subtype noun, a color/
// multicolored/colorless adjective, the "other"/"another" self-exclusion) —
// the `crate::parsers::condition` routing's Predicate-slot vocabulary.
//
// Template: "you control ${0}" renders the object noun with its indefinite
// article (`crates/plugin/src/render/condition.rs`'s `exists_phrase`
// — the generic slot filler can't supply "a"/"an", so this shape gets a
// hand-written render arm on the CORE `Exists` variant, not the macro
// template).
//
// Usage: YouControl(Type(Artifact)) / YouControl(And([Permanent,
// Subtype(Human)])).
(
    name: "YouControl",
    template: "you control ${0}",
    kinds: [Condition],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: Exists(And([And([Permanent, Param(0)]), ControlledBy(Ref(You))])),
)
